		{
			"id": "link-24288a242182412a2c095ed767e78116",
			"title": "Tell HN: I'm 60 years old. Claude Code has re-ignited a passion",
			"link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47282777",
			"contents": "<div class=\"Story_container\"><div class=\"Story_data\"><div class=\"Story_title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47282777\"><span>Tell HN: I'm 60 years old. Claude Code has re-ignited a passion</span></a></div><div class=\"Story_meta\"><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47282777\">1063 points</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=shannoncc\"><span>shannoncc</span></a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47282777\">4 days ago</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47282777\">968 comments</a></span><div class=\"Story_comment\"><span>I’m ready to retire. In my younger days, I remember a few pivotal moments for me as a young nerd. Active Server Pages. COM components. VB6. I know these are laughable today but back then it was the greatest thing in the world to be able to call server-side commands. It kept me up nights trying to absorb it all. Fast forward decades and Claude Code is giving me that same energy and drive. I love it. It feels like it did back then. I’m chasing the midnight hour and not getting any sleep.</span></div></div></div></div>",
			"retrieved": 1772893487488
		},
